    "paper": "L. W. Whitlow, S. Rock, A. Bodek, E. M. Riordan, S. Dasu, 'A precise extraction of R = sigma_L/sigma_T from a global analysis of the SLAC deep inelastic e-p and e-d scattering cross sections', Phys. Lett. B 250 (1990) 193, doi:10.1016/0370-2693(90)91176-C (read: PolarizedLithiumSim/refs/whitlow1990_R.pdf, the SLAC-PUB-5284 preprint)",
    "publishing_convention": "R is a RATIO (convention-free). Tables 3-13 are 'R' for e-p and e-d combined: the paper (p. 6) averaged the extracted R_p and R_d in each (x, Q2) bin into a single R after finding R_d - R_p = -0.001 +- 0.009 (stat) +- 0.009 (sys) (its Eq. (5); this record's Table 1, kept under body.rd_minus_rp). R is extracted at the bin centre after a bin-centring correction (p. 5). The letter does not print the numerical table ('given in ref. 11', a thesis), so the record cannot be cross-checked against the letter.",
    "errors": "stat and sys separately, symmetric, absolute; the paper's systematic includes a radiative-correction uncertainty correlated with epsilon (+-0.025 in R, p. 4) and normalisation factors N_i that are 'strongly correlated' (p. 5); no covariance is given.",
